{"author":"rebar review bot","author_email":"rebar-review-bot@rebar.solutions.navateam.com","data":{"body":"## Metric source for the replacement alarm (AC6)\n\nThe alarm `lmn-staging-private-context-denied` keeps its name, so the\noperator-facing signal is stable, but its metric source changed from a raw\nAWS/S3 metric to a derived one.\n\n**Old source (mis-scoped):** `AWS/S3` `4xxErrors`, dimensions\n`BucketName=lmn-staging-private-context-896586841071`,\n`FilterId=all-private-context-requests`. That metric counts every 4xx against\nthe bucket, so it counted the deliberate negative-access probes the\n`lmn-staging-private-audit-*` runner issues. On 2026-09-18 the worst\n300-second windows held 49 and 45 403s, of which 45 were audit denials in each\n— the audit floor alone clears the old `Sum > 5` threshold nine times over.\n\n**New source:** S3 server access logs delivered to\n`s3://lmn-staging-private-context-logs-896586841071/access/`, parsed by the\n`lmn-private-context-denied-metric` Lambda on a `rate(5 minutes)` EventBridge\nschedule, published as:\n\n- namespace: `lmn/staging`\n- metric name: `private_context_unexpected_denials`\n- statistic `Sum`, period 300, threshold `> 5`, 1 evaluation period,\n  `treat_missing_data = notBreaching`\n\nRecords counted:\n\n```\nbucket      = lmn-staging-private-context-896586841071\nhttp_status = 403\nerror_code  = AccessDenied\nrequester NOT LIKE arn:aws:sts::896586841071:assumed-role/*/lmn-staging-private-audit-*\nrequester  != arn:aws:iam::896586841071:user/joe_frontier\n```\n\nServer access logs are best-effort delayed delivery, so the alarm detects a\ndenial burst after delivery rather than at request time. The account has no\nCloudTrail trail and no event data store, so S3 data-event denials are not\nvisible there today; a data-event trail would give request-time detection and\nis the upgrade path if the delivery delay proves too slow.\n\n**What was deliberately NOT done:** the threshold was not raised (that hides\nreal denials behind a moving audit floor), and the audited application roles\nwere not added to the bucket-policy allowlist (the policy is the control the\naudit exists to verify). The change adds three new files and modifies no\nexisting file, so every bucket-policy restriction is untouched.\n\nLanded as Gerrit change 3017, commit `204c60697b8d2468e35f3168ae008c63c87e780f`."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789935729320232001,"uuid":"7bc52cff-9016-4714-82d9-45cd067d4be2"}